WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.112 --> 00:00:06.698
Okay, so the agent design space maps how production agents cluster around their constraints rather than neat types.

2
00:00:06.698 --> 00:00:09.553
A single-loop agent retrieves context,

3
00:00:09.703 --> 00:00:11.633
calls a tool and answers,

4
00:00:11.713 --> 00:00:15.578
which fits a docs-search assistant where wrong answers cost little.

5
00:00:15.578 --> 00:00:21.773
Multi-turn, workflow, supervisor and persistent-goal agents run progressively longer,

6
00:00:21.853 --> 00:00:24.555
so more of their state must survive a restart.

7
00:00:24.555 --> 00:00:27.380
So the design space isn't a menu,

8
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.303
and the mistake is stretching a simple pattern past its scope.

9
00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:32.498
For a new agent,

10
00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.193
I ask whether it acts or just generates,

11
00:00:35.293 --> 00:00:37.753
keeps state, or needs several agents.
